  "question": "What is the minimal CouncilSpec v2 root envelope such that every one of the 58 protocol records and 72 preset records in 12-COUNCIL-PROTOCOLS-AND-PRESETS.json validates against it, AND a v1 Council Charter document (13 properties, 12 required) migrates forward with zero information loss - and which v1 property must change shape for that to be true?",
  "answer": "The minimal v2 root envelope is a Draft 2020-12 oneOf over three strict record types (charter_v2, protocol_record, preset_record) sharing $defs for the overlapping axes. Catalogue records validate unchanged because protocol/preset branches accept their existing keys and the caps-shaped stopping object. A v1 charter migrates by wrapping stopping: the v1 string $defs.stopping_expr becomes {mode:expression, expression:<string>}. No v1 property is dropped; that wrap is the only shape change. A discriminated union without that wrap cannot accept both a v1 charter and the catalogue stopping object under one named property.",
